   1.9 "Built Product" means any deliverable that is designed, built,
       tested, verified, simulated or documented with the help of the
       Software and whose primary purpose is not to provide the
       engineering-tooling functionality described in section 1.8.
       Built Products include, for example, hardware products, printed
       circuit boards, enclosures and mechanical parts, firmware,
       embedded and application software, simulations and digital twins
